From ae71bf075d38f1e02e2676e9ea81f46578d74f86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qwqgong-ui <248246420+qwqgong-ui@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 13:16:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] androidcyaml: rebuild the integration facade as the single
 seam

The facade covered four functions while the AndroidCyaml wrapper imported
fourteen mihomo packages directly, so every upstream rename in any of them
broke a downstream repository with no way to see it coming.

Rebuild it by capability domain -- config, lifecycle, network, process,
transport, diagnostics -- so the wrapper imports this package and nothing
else, and add FacadeVersion so a contract change fails the consumer's build
instead of misbehaving on a device. The sync guidance moves from README.md
into doc.go, next to the contract it describes.

Three neutral changes underneath it:

component/process publishes its endpoint resolver atomically. A core
restarted in-process writes it from the start and stop paths while rule
evaluation reads it on the hot path, which is a data race on a plain package
variable. It also exposes whether a resolver is installed, so the tunnel can
skip the FindPackageName call that follows a successful endpoint lookup --
that resolver already returned the package name, making the second lookup
either identical work or, with no name resolver registered, a guaranteed
error once per matched connection.

component/dialer exports EnvironmentScope so an embedder can address a scope
it created rather than rebuilding the string by hand.

dns gains EvictNetworkScope. Scoped keys are why a handover clears nothing:
each network's answers stay addressable under their own branch. Retirement is
the case that leaves behind -- when the platform stops tracking a network its
branch has no owner, yet the answers survive to their own expiry, a 24-hour
floor with no profile left to explain them.
